// REJECTS: Field 'class' is required
//
// A JsonModelConnection requires class and url. Its grammar is one shared
// `definition: (modelConnectionClass | connectionUrl | modelChainMappings)* EOF` covering
// Json, Xml AND ModelChain connections, so nothing in the .g4 distinguishes them at all.
//
// That sharing is also where legend-engine is permissive: `mappings:` on a
// JsonModelConnection and `class:` on a ModelChainConnection both parse and are silently
// discarded. Only the required-field check does any work here.
###Connection
JsonModelConnection fixture::neg::JsonWithoutClass
{
   url: 'model://fixture/person.json';
}
